    "created_at": "2022-07-28T18:17:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-07-28T18:17:13Z",
    "body": "> According to MDN the send method enqueues data of supported types for transfer, however the data is not queued across a variety of user agents.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what this sentence means. The [standard text](https://websockets.spec.whatwg.org/#dom-websocket-send) doesn't explicitly say that the data is queued, but it's very clear that either the data is sent or the connection is closed. The standard text may be a little bit unclear, but queuing is the only reasonable implementation.\r\n\r\n> When data is not queued a transmission payload is abandoned from transfer if in conflict with a more recent transmission.\r\n\r\nI don't understand this either. Messages are sent in strict order.",
